<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar vessel movements on July 30.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar vessel movements on July 30.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Independent surveyors detailed Thai sugar freight movement as follows (in tonne tel quels):</p>
<p>Vessel		  Position	  Quantity    Destination</p>
<p>Friendship	    SLD Jly 27	18,900	Japan</p>
<p>Amodelmar	     SLD Jly 25	 3,000	China</p>
<p>Perovomaisk	   SLD Jly 25	10,500	S.Korea</p>
<p>Orient Express	SLD Jly 24	 1,200	Cambodia</p>
<p>Sangthai Radium     SLD Jly 26	   500	Singapore</p>
<p>Fortune Navigator   ETD Jly 28	 5,000	Vietnam</p>
<p>Burgos		  ETD Aug 03	14,000	Vladivostok</p>
<p>Jutha Suphannika    N/A		 12,000	Japan</p>
<p>Navigator D	   ETD Aug 01	12,500	Japan</p>
<p>Gang Nam		ETD Aug 31	 5,000	India</p>
<p>Tasmia		  N/A		 12,000	Mombaza</p>
<p>Alam Tangkas	  ETA Aug 01	15,000	Malaysia</p>
<p>Dibena Express	ETB Jly 29	 7,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Chong Cong Gang     CANCELLED</p>
<p>Yuan Jiang	    N/A		 14,000	Pakistan</p>
<p>Bong Hoa San	  ETD Aug 30	   400	N.Korea</p>
<p>Jutha Buddharaksa   ETA Aug 04	12,000	Japan</p>
<p>Am Nok Gang	   ETA Jly 31	10,800	Indonesia</p>
<p>RCL-A		   ETA Aug 03	 1,100	Indonesia</p>
<p>NOTE: SLD indicates that the vessel has left, ETA = Estimated Time of Arrival, ETD = Estimated Time of Departure, ETR = Estimated Time of Readiness, L/CAN indicated period when vessels are expected in for loading or be cancelled.</p>
</text>
